  Not using GPU by default - this policy is a tiny MLP (few thousand params); CPU<->GPU transfer overhead makes GPU SLOWER here, not faster. Pass --device cuda to force it anyway.
  When this actually matters as the project scales: bigger policy_kwargs net_arch, a CNN/graph encoder over topology structure, or (the bigger lever, matters before GPU does) vectorizing many parallel envs with SubprocVecEnv instead of one env per run - that's what actually saturates a GPU for RL at this problem scale, not a single tiny MLP forward pass.

